WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Wednesday, halfway through the trading week, welcome to modern investing techniques,

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:11.900
episode 48. It's May 20th, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver. Midweek, let's reassess this week's

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.860
positions and look for fresh setups. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.540
and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.400
I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.240
before putting real money to work. Canadian investors holding heavy TFSA positions and growth names

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:41.200
should watch the 10-year treasury yield at 4.69%, because it is already repricing long duration

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:49.860
assets faster than earnings can offset. Markets closed lower today with the S&amp;P 500 at 7,354,

00:00:50.420 --> 00:01:03.060
down 0.7%. The NASDAQ composite finished at 25,871, down 0.8%. The TSX composite closed at 33,741,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.820
down 0.3%. Sticky long-end yields near 52-week highs are shaping sentiment,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.520
along with anticipation around tomorrow's in-bedia earnings.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.980
Fresh options flow shows institutions harvesting elevated implied volatility on NBDA,

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:26.320
while broader macro concerns around energy inflation linger. That yield pressure sets up

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.020
evaluation opportunity worth examining more closely. PayPal's depressed valuation combined

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:38.500
with $6 billion in annual free cash flow creates a classic buyback compounding setup that retail

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:44.180
investors can replicate using simple screens. At roughly 6.5 times free cash flow,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:50.420
in a $40 billion market cap, the company can retire a meaningful percentage of shares each year

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:55.860
while the multiple stays compressed. The strategy works by holding through the period of depressed

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:01.620
sentiment, letting the shrinking share count do the heavy lifting. Then you wait for a re-rating once

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:07.720
the market stops treating the business as structurally broken. Implementation is straightforward. Screen

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:14.020
for companies with stable or growing free cash flow, buyback authorization above 10% of market cap,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:20.060
and forward price to earnings below 12. Historical parallels include mature pairs in the early

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:27.120
2000s-10s that delivered multi-bagger returns once sentiment normalized. The main risk is continued

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.800
competitive pressure on branded checkout, which could erode the cash flow base the thesis relies on.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:39.340
That same PayPal setup is also the basis for today's practice investment. This is a simulated

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:47.280
trade for educational purposes only with no real money involved. Today's pick is PYPL, PayPal holdings

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:53.760
incorporated on the NASDAQ in the financial sector. The strategy is a valuation play on durable

00:02:53.760 --> 00:03:00.200
free cash flow and aggressive buybacks at depressed multiples. This is the same day flash trade only.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:06.320
The catalyst comes from a reddit deep dive highlighting over $6 billion in annual free cash flow

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.140
at a 6.5 times multiple and potential share count reduction that the market is ignoring.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.260
The technical setup shows the stock trading well below historical averages. Risk assessment points

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:23.680
to competitive pressure from Apple Pay and Stripe that could pressure margins, so the stop would be

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:31.500
placed at 8% below entry to capital loss. The target is plus 2% to plus 4% on re-rating momentum

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:37.720
if sentiment shifts. Confidence level is medium because durable cash flow and buyback math are

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:44.600
clear, but sector rotation into higher beta names remains a wild card. This trade demonstrates how

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:50.700
to quantify a buyback yield and compare it against current valuation to identify asymmetric setups

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:57.100
that index funds miss. Listeners learn to separate narrative price action from the actual capital

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:03.300
return math that drives long-term compounding. While we wait on that flash outcome, here is how

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:09.460
yesterday's weekly hold played out. Last week's simulated hold was ACM on an infrastructure

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:16.400
consulting contract win that provided multi-year revenue visibility. Entry came at $80 and

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:25.220
9 cents on Monday's open and exit at $71 on Friday's close. The result was a loss of 11.35%

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:34.100
or $113.50 on a $1,000 position. The multi-year visibility from the contract was real, yet the

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:40.680
position still suffered when capital rotated into higher beta AI names. This produced negative alpha

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:47.200
of roughly 10.5% over the holding window. What this teaches us is the need for volume confirmation

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:53.380
above the 20-day average before entering momentum trades on earnings beats. Learning from that rotation

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:58.940
risk, let us examine a deeper structural issue many Canadian investors face. Imagine you just

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:06.040
re-balanced your TFSA and notice 42% of the equity sleeve sits in Canadian names because you understand

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:12.000
the banks and energy names better. That allocation feels prudent until you compare it to Canada's

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:19.400
actual 3% weight in global market capitalization. The mechanism driving the mismatch is simple. Your job,

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:27.420
home, and pension already embed heavy Canada exposure, so adding another 30-50% in TSX stocks doubles

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:33.540
down on the same two sectors that make up half the index. Professionals routinely check global market

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:40.100
cap weights first, then apply a modest home bias tilt only for the dividend tax credit and currency

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:47.480
hedging benefits. The biggest misconception is that familiarity reduces risk. Instead, it concentrates

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:54.680
sector and currency risk that a simple 20% Canadian equity cap would materially lower. With that allocation

00:05:54.680 --> 00:06:01.460
discipline in mind, here are a few tools that can sharpen execution. On usual whales, surfaces real time

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:07.600
institutional options sweeps and unusual activity that retail traders can use to gauge where smart money

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:13.520
is placing bets ahead of catalysts. It gives an edge by highlighting large premium collections or

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:19.880
aggressive put-selling that often precedes support levels, something most screeners miss. Any investor

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:24.940
comfortable with options chains should start with the retail subscription tier that includes Mr. Whale

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:32.540
Alerts. Options play NVDA flow tracker breaks down specific institutional put-sales with exact strikes,

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.620
premiums collected, and notional risk, allowing listeners to map support zones the market is pricing

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:44.620
in. It is most useful for earnings week positioning where implied volatility crush can reward short

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:50.460
volatility trades even without directional conviction. Access it directly through the options play

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:56.260
Twitter feed or their platform dashboard. While you explore those platforms, here are three quick

00:06:56.260 --> 00:07:03.040
items worth watching. Meta begins its latest round of layoffs impacting approximately 8,000 employees.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.880
The move continues the company's efficiency drive and could free up cash for buybacks or AI

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:15.700
infrastructure spend. Add media to your watch list for post-layoff margin expansion signals on next

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:21.900
earnings. Exxon mobile and chevron both closed higher for seven straight sessions. The streak shows

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:27.260
sustained institutional interest in integrated energy names despite broader market rotation.

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:33.260
Trim and the overweight energy positions if the streak breaks on volume below the 20-day average.

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:40.300
Foreclosures fell 8% month over month but remain up 18% year over year. The mixed housing data

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:45.920
suggests consumer stress is rising slowly rather than spiking. Avoid adding Canadian

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:53.660
REIT exposure this week until the trend stabilizes. Our simulated portfolio across 20 trades shows a 55%

00:07:53.660 --> 00:08:02.040
win rate with 11 wins, 8 losses, and 1 break even. Cumulative profit and loss sits at negative $4.66.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:10.780
Average return per trade is negative 0.02%, with the best trade of plus 13.36%,

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:16.340
and a worst trade of negative 11.35%. The current streak is one loss,

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:22.620
and our AI analysis is learning from sector rotation patterns and adjusting position sizing accordingly.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:28.740
Before we wrap, open your brokerage screener, set free cash flow yield above 8%,

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:34.800
